  --- the verdict ---
  [the short anchor alone accounts for 76% of the bounding]
  THE BOUNDING IS REAL AND IT IS NOT A FRAME. Both pre-registered halves
  pass -- drift down, per-cycle excursion above the no-integrator floor --
  and the surviving controls say the jaw is not what did it:
    - the short anchor alone buys most of the bounding
    - the creature's own silences schedule it just as well
  What the run establishes is a fact about the DECODER: an intermittent hard
  anchor beats both a long anchor and a continuous leak, and
  `f1_return_tau_ms` at 633 ms was far too long. The jaw is ONE schedule for
  that anchor and not a privileged one, so `the jaw cycle is a boundary for
  F1` is REFUSED and the useful finding is a mis-set constant.
